In article <1991Jan28.182421.25008@digibd.com> merlyn@digibd.com (Brian Westley (Merlyn LeRoy)) writes:
>Scroll of duplication
>    Allows you to duplicate an item.  Caveats with wands of wishing, etc.
>    If you duplicate itself, you can "save" it, since the original
>    vanishes.  Just gives you 1 more of the item, if you duplicate
>    3 knives.  Cursed ought to make a cursed duplicate & destroy the
>    original.  Should Blessed make a blessed copy?

Maybe Blessed scrolls should make 1-4 copies (at random) instead of a blessed
copy. Don't forget named weapons, too... anybody trying to duplicate
Stormbringer should get a nasty surprise (maybe the original and the clone
"cancel each other out" in a large explosion?)
 
>Wand of clone monster
>    Obvious.  Cloning a mimic produces a "hiding" mimic, in case
>    the room is dark...  "Blessed" should make many clones.

I like this idea. Cloned monsters should have the same attitude (tame,
peaceful) as the original - except for cursed wands, which make the clone
instantly aggressive... Should we be allowed to clone shopkeepers?

>Wand of everything
>    This is a fun one, but a bit tricky to implement.  When zapped,
>    it picks a random wand effect and does that.  The tricky part is
>    "identifying" it as, say, a wand of digging on the first zap,
>    and then as a wand of everything on a subsequent zap.  Easiest
>    way around this is to simply identify it as whatever it was
>    zapped as most recently, and let the player name it.

Ah, the Wand of Wonder from Moria. I'd _love_ to see this in NH, especially
in conjunction with the next wand...

>Wand of fireballs
>    I had changed the wand of fire to zap a distance, then
>    explode, thus:
>         \!/
>    @----=*=
>         /!\

Isn't something like this being done in 3.1?

>Wand of lightning
>    I had changed this to be accurate at 2 squares, chancier at
>    farther distances, by doing:
>        ---
>    @---   --
>	     ---

That's nasty! In that case, lightning blasts from dragons (whatever colour it
may be) should be prone to this, too (but maybe only after a longer distance)
Red dragons should be able to spit fireballs, too.

>Ring of wand charges
>    Ring with a few zaps in it.  When you zap an empty wand, the
>    ring glows and gives the wand a free zap.  Shouldn't work for
>    wishing, of course.

How about having a blessed ring give the wand an _extra_ zap, so you zap a
wand with 0 charges, get the zap and the wand ends up with 1 charge, to boot.

>A book "+" might be a volume of "Magic Potions A-L" instead of plaid, etc.
>Reading it will identify potions starting with A-L, i.e. you now know
>what color a "healing" potion is, a "blindness" potion, but it won't
>tell you the color of "paralysis", etc.  Two volumes each for
>potions, scroll, rings, wands.  Make them rare...

I'd like to see this one, too. This sort of thing should be EXPENSIVE if you
find one in a shop. Perhaps there should be a limit of one of each book per
game (as with named weapons) so you could end up having to fight a shopkeeper
to get his book of identification...

>I would sometimes put guardian monsters inside chests (appropriate
>ones only) that come out aggravated.  floating eyes, bats, rats,
>snakes, gremins, etc. would all be good.

Like the djinni and the ghost from the potion bottles? Naturally, there is a
good chance that the monster has damaged the contents of the chest.

You open the chest -more-
The Wizard of Yendor emerges from the chest... -more- 

>Chests should occasionally contain all of the same type of object
>(all potions, all scrolls, etc).  A good gag that I pulled was
>a chest of chests would only contain chests of chests, that is,

I don't like the idea of chests of chests from a programming point of view,
but then I ain't writing the code anyway. From a player's point of view, I can
see it being VERY irritating, especially if some chests are trapped and some
contain monsters...

Incidentally, has anyone noticed that empty chests always seem to be the
hardest to break open? :-)

>Blessed scroll of amnesia should make you forget what all the types
>of magic are (i.e. you forget that a blue potion is healing, or whatever).
>You, of course, forget what scroll is amnesia, too.

Surely a cursed scroll should do this?

>Blessed ring of teleport control should allow you to zap a monster
>with teleportation and control where it lands.

And blessed rings of polymorph control should allow you to choose what to
polymorph it into...

What do you want to polymorph Asidonhopo into? grid bug

hee hee hee...

